n Russia and I just love put  in because he's the greatest communist  of all time your audience is gonna go  like oh my god congra is so terrible  poor Russia but I know for sure they  don't know that Russia is not a  communist country at all do you believe  that when you hear in the American press  that the Russians had something to do  with the election  that sounds really funny to me because  wow I don't think that Russia would  would have done that I don't think that  is the job of the media nowadays to say  the truth it's mostly emotional I mean  if we have the media sensational not  Arab emotion exactly and then to react  to the media from from from other  media's around the world so do you feel  that's true for Russian media as well  yes all media yes exactly  do you think Putin has been in power too  long yes because sometimes I'm feeling  that he's becoming a bit inadequate and  adequate yeah and probably he stops  understanding what he wants what he's  doing and this is frightening for such a  level of authority I disagree with him  on many points yes but mostly satisfied  with the current political system yes  how are you different than the older  generation people who were born in the  Soviet Union  they didn't have a chance to travel  around the world we had this chance  because the borders are open and the  Western pop culture coming to us as  Russians do you feel isolated for  serious still got YouTube we watch CBS  watch Marvel will watch HBO our  favorites series is like Game of Thrones  right no you cannot isolate us because  we got money and we got we can grab a  ticket and visit you if you want but we  are ok here right for serious Alex  Wagner is with us at the table so  interesting to hear their perspectives  and certainly on Trump did they feel as  free and open to talk about their own  leader President Putin you know there's  a real sense of defiance that I got from  not just the Russian Millennials I spoke  with but Russians on the street  I